# LLM provider API keys
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The router tries Anthropic first, then OpenAI, then falls back to
# StubRouter (offline / no API calls). To use a real provider, set ONE
# of the env vars below and `pip install` the matching SDK
# (uncomment the line in requirements.txt).
#
#   export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
#   export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
#
# The keys are read implicitly by the SDKs — never paste them into
# source, into a chat message, or into a GitHub issue. The `.env` file
# is gitignored.
#
# The StubRouter needs no key. It returns template-based content for
# all 4 streams, which is enough to demo the dashboard end-to-end and
# to pass the 105-test suite.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Anthropic (Claude) — recommended for cost. ~$0.04/day at 40 calls/day.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# OpenAI (GPT) — alternative. Pick one of the two.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the default model. Defaults are claude-3-5-haiku
# and gpt-4o-mini. If you set HUSTLE_LLM_PROVIDER=stub, the offline
# router is used regardless of which key (if any) is set.
# HUSTLE_LLM_PROVIDER=stub
